{"Tests use brittle time.sleep(0.1) and assertions on internal structure making them flaky and tightly coupled to implementation": 0.3147110044956207, "SpansBuffer.__reduce__ discards runtime state (compression, client) when sent to child processes - if parent process had trained a compression dictionary or populated cached resources, that state will be lost in child processes which get fresh compressors/clients": 0.24448683857917786, "Multiprocess flusher refactor risks lost/duplicated segments on crash - if a process crashes between producing to Kafka and calling done_flush_segments, segments may be lost or duplicated": 0.7242648601531982, "_ensure_processes_alive has off-by-one error in restart counter check - it checks MAX_PROCESS_RESTARTS before incrementing the counter, potentially allowing one additional undesired restart": 0.28068310022354126, "_ensure_processes_alive may have race conditions if called concurrently with other lifecycle operations when killing and recreating processes": 0.18306054174900055, "Parent uses per-process SpansBuffer instances for memory checks and stored-segment metrics that can be stale or inconsistent with what children are actively deleting, leading to incorrect backpressure or pause decisions": 0.6206584572792053, "join() calls process.terminate() but never calls process.join() afterwards, which can leave defunct zombie processes on Unix systems": 0.799860954284668, "Tests only cover threaded path (produce_to_pipe) and never exercise the real multiprocessing/spawn path": 0.4171436131000519}